Z||000000||80's BOY||04-21-2000||11:29 AM||||is it worth pulling the tank out of my 85 gt to put in an aftermarket fuel pump. i have a stroked 2.8, and my fuel pressure is not up to par. about 35-40 under load. i heard that an iroc z pump will fit and give me performance. or should i just put on a regulator to "pinch" off the return line? i would really like to try the camaro pump along with larger injectors, since it is only about $60 or so for a new one through a local parts store. any advice would help. you guys have been a great help so far so if this would be wasted effort, i'd like to find out the easy way first without laying upside down in my yard for an hour.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Phil||04-21-2000||12:29 PM||||You might try putting in an adjustable fuel pressure regulator in place of the stock non adjst. one.||||reg||1
Z||000002||80's BOY||04-21-2000||12:50 PM||||i'm not very impressed with the stock replacement for an adjustable regulator. how do you get a wrench on it when it is so far under the plenum?? are there any other regulators that would fit in any other locations?||||reg||1
Z||000003||1FST2M6||04-21-2000||01:02 PM||||I had an NOS, a Stillen unit and now have an Vortech FMU. controlling my fuel pressure. The NOS unit was nice cause it had all the parts... just screws into the return line by the battery. the stillen unit was ok but was slow to release and held my fuel pressure up when i didn't need it.. the SFMU is responsive and well worth the money. I paid $267 after tax... (I got a sweet deal)  The hypertech one will work ok... both Snap-on and Craftsman make ratcheting closed end wrenches that will work the top of a pressure regulator just fine... i have an IROC fuel pump in my car...  how much did they quote you?!?! I got NAILED on mine... over $200. it is new right.. your not gunna get a reman unit are ya... If your gunna spend the time and money just do it once, by making sure your getting new parts. I've been there on other cars... may be cheaper for the same thing but there was a reason it was returned in the first place... ||||reg||1
Z||000004||1FST2M6||04-21-2000||01:04 PM||||another thing.. you might just need to rebuild the stock one and you might be ok... place a penny under the diaphram for an increase in fuel pressure! about 3-7psi ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Eric||04-21-2000||03:23 PM||||Try the coin trick and save $90.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Fret Naught||04-21-2000||03:27 PM||||A penny saved is a penny earned!!!!!||||reg||7
